# Generated / vendored
node_modules/
coverage/
package-lock.json

# Generated by `npm run types` from the JSDoc in lib/ — tsc owns the formatting,
# and test/unit/types.test.js byte-compares against exactly what tsc emitted.
types/

# Prettier's Handlebars parser rejects `{{> "partial"}}`, which every template
# in this repo relies on — it errors rather than formatting. Templates are
# hand-formatted.
*.hbs

# A verbatim copy of .claude/skills/session-reflect/rubric.md, shipped beside the
# kiss-branch-close skill so a consuming site scores its reflections against the same
# rubric. test/unit/plugin-manifests.test.js byte-compares it against the
# original past its one-line source header — prettier reflowing the copy alone
# would break that identity.
plugins/kiss-memory/skills/kiss-branch-close/rubric.md

# Written by `npx kiss-ssg aikb 9-migrated-from-v1.js` and committed as the
# exemplar. `JSON.stringify(map, null, 2)` puts one value per line where
# prettier would fill a short array onto one, and the engine cannot depend on
# prettier at run time — so the machine-written JSON is left as the engine
# writes it. The markdown beside it *is* emitted prettier-clean (tables padded
# the way prettier pads them), and the authored notes under AIKB/notes/ are
# ordinary source, so neither is ignored.
examples/9-migrated-from-v1/AIKB/*.json

# Written by `npx kiss-ssg aikb 11-blog.js` and committed, for the same reason.
examples/11-blog/AIKB/*.json

# The artifact example 12 was converted from, kept exactly as it arrived. It is
# input, not source: formatting it would change the thing the conversion is
# measured against, and `tools/compare.mjs` compares the built page to this file.
examples/12-from-a-single-file/source/

# The artifact's stylesheet, copied in whole by `tools/convert.mjs` and committed
# as it emits it. Prettier would normalise the values inside — `.9fr` to
# `0.9fr`, `clamp(a,b,c)` to `clamp(a, b, c)` — and the point of copying it whole
# is that the browser gets the stylesheet the artifact had. Formatting it would
# make the committed file differ from what the conversion produces.
examples/12-from-a-single-file/src/assets/css/
